      "narrative": "The resolution succeeds \u2014 Kael's investigation yields results. I'll narrate the narrow success.\n\n**Mara Venn** tilts her head, a faint crease forming between her brows. \"Before it was filed? The lock wasn't maintained by one person. It was a guild rotation \u2014 the Kestrel Guild sent a different lockwright every season to oil the tumblers and check the bearings.\" She taps a finger on the table. \"Toran was the last one on that rotation. He'd know the names of the ones before him.\"\n\nShe glances at the clerk again, but something flickers in her expression \u2014 a hesitation. She's given you the guild rotation fact, but the list of names, the sequence of who handled it across those years... she's holding that back. Not deliberately, perhaps. She simply doesn't have it all at the tip of her tongue.\n\n\"The Kestrel Guild's records would have the full roster,\" she adds, almost as an afterthought. \"If those still exist.\"\n\nShe watches you, waiting to see if that's enough or if you'll press further."
