      "narrative": "The press of your question hangs in the air. Mara Venn's eyes narrow \u2014 not at you, but past you, as if sifting through old memory. Her lips part.\n\nThen Toran Vex clears his throat, a thin, reedy sound.\n\n\"Ah \u2014 I wouldn't \u2014 that's not \u2014\" He fumbles with his ink-stained cuffs, tugging at the fabric. \"Passage wasn't *sold*, exactly. Not like a ferry ticket. It was... granted. By arrangement. Old Bram kept a ledger, but he was the only one who ever handled the transactions.\"\n\nMara Venn's gaze snaps to him, sharp and sudden. \"Toran.\"\n\nHe flinches. \"I'm just \u2014 that's how it worked. Bram took the payments. No one else touched that side of things.\" He swallows. \"And Bram's dead.\"\n\nThe word lands like a stone in still water. Mara Venn's jaw tightens. She turns back to you, and there's something careful in her expression now \u2014 a door that's just been pulled ajar and then, very deliberately, held in place.\n\n\"Toran's right,\" she says, her voice flat. \"Bram handled the payments. Alone. Whatever names were in that ledger went with him.\"\n\nShe holds your gaze, but her fingers have gone still around her cup. The question sat poorly with her \u2014 or perhaps the answer did. You can't tell which.\n\nThe silence stretches. Neither of them offers more."
    },
